75 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Queen consists of several interconnected components that work together to process, validate, mine, and propagate transactions across the peer-to-peer network. The Wallet manages keys and creates digitally signed transactions. The Transaction component constructs transactions using available UTXOs and prepares them for broadcast. The Node receives transactions and blocks from peers and independently validates them according to the consensus rules implemented by the system. Valid transactions are maintained in the mempool and can later be selected by the Mining component to construct a new block and perform Proof-of- Work. After a block is produced, it is verified again before being added to the local blockchain and applied to the UTXO set. The Blockchain and Consensus components provide the rules used to determine whether transactions and blocks are valid, allowing each node to independently calculate and verify the state of the chain. This architecture separates user operations, transaction processing, mining, networking, and consensus logic while keeping the validation rules consistent across participating nodes.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
76 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Transactions are validated independently by nodes before entering the mempool, while mined blocks are independently validated before updating the blockchain and UTXO state.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
