/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (Figure 2 illustrates the basic data structure of the Queen blockchain and the relationship between blocks, transactions, and the UTXO state. Each block contains the information required to identify its position in the chain, link it to the previous block, verify its Proof-of-Work, and validate its transaction set. The transaction list contains individual transactions identified by their TXIDs, with each transaction consisting of inputs and outputs. Inputs reference previously created UTXOs through a transaction ID and output index, while outputs define a new address and amount that can become an available UTXO. When a transaction is accepted, its referenced UTXOs are marked as spent and its outputs are added to the UTXO state. During block validation, the node independently checks the transactions and their referenced UTXOs before applying the resulting state changes to its local ledger. This structure allows the current spendable state of the blockchain to be derived from the transaction history rather than relying on a separate balance record.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
