/E (Figure 3 illustrates the transaction and UTXO flow in Queen. A transaction references existing UTXOs through their transaction IDs and output indexes. The node verifies the referenced UTXOs, checks ownership through the public key, and verifies the transaction signature before accepting the transaction. The total value of the referenced inputs must be equal to or greater than the total value of the outputs, with the difference treated as the transaction fee. Duplicate inputs and already-spent or nonexistent UTXOs are rejected. Once validated, the transaction enters the mempool and can later be included in a mined block. After the block is accepted, the referenced UTXOs are marked as spent and the transaction outputs become new UTXOs available for future transactions.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
