/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Queen uses digital signatures to authorize the spending of previously created UTXOs. Each transaction input contains a reference to a previous transaction output, a public key, and a digital signature. Before verification, Queen constructs a deterministic transaction payload containing the transaction version, input references, outputs, fee, timestamp, and message. The signature itself is not included in this payload. The serialized payload is hashed using double SHA-256 to produce the message digest used for signature verification. The public key supplied by the input is converted into an address, and the resulting address must match the address stored in the referenced UTXO. The node then verifies the signature against the calculated digest using the secp256k1 elliptic curve and DER signature decoding. If any of these checks fail, the transaction is rejected.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
