114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (Queen uses CPU-based Proof-of-Work to determine whether a candidate block satisfies the current mining difficulty. The miner first constructs a block containing the block metadata and selected transactions. The block header is serialized and processed to generate a seed, which is then supplied to the CPU mining algorithm. Multiple workers can search different nonce sequences concurrently. For each nonce, the mining algorithm produces a resulting hash that is compared with the required difficulty target. Mining succeeds when the resulting hash satisfies the target condition. The successful nonce and hash are then stored in the block. When the block is received by another node, the node independently reconstructs the required header and performs the same computation to verify the reported result before accepting the block.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
