/P 64 0 R
/E (A block received by a Queen node is independently validated before being added to the local blockchain. The node checks the previous block reference, block structure, Proof-of-Work, transaction validity, Merkle root, and UTXO state. Each transaction is verified independently, including its inputs, outputs, signatures, and referenced UTXOs. Blocks containing invalid transactions, invalid Proof-of-Work, inconsistent Merkle roots, or invalid chain references are rejected. This process allows nodes to reach agreement on the valid chain without relying on trust in the miner.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
